<title>UK: GOLF-NORMAN REGAINS TOP SPOT.</title>
<headline>GOLF-NORMAN REGAINS TOP SPOT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greg Norman regained his world number one ranking with his second place finish in the Spanish Open on Sunday, just one week after he lost it to American Tom Lehman.</p>
<p>The Australian lost the Spanish Open in a playoff against Mark James of Britain, a Ryder Cup player who climbed into the top 100 in 91st place.</p>
<p>The new positions released on Monday had former world number one Nick Price of Zimbabwe improving one place to third, above Steve Elkington of Australia.</p>
<p>Masters champion Tiger Woods remained fifth.</p>
